kunzite (SM6475 parrot): the topaz key driver on kunzite's PMICs.
Boot #13 faulted in sweet_keys_init: topaz's SM6225 arbiter addresses do not
exist here. kunzite has PMIC arbiter v7 (live FDT spmi@c42d000: cnfg
0xc42d000, core 0xc400000, obsrvr 0xc440000), so: APID map at core +
0x2000 + 4n, owner at cnfg + 4n, observer channel 0x20 * apid (Linux 6.6
spmi-pmic-arb.c v7 ops), version 0x7xxxxxxx, up to 1024 APIDs. Keys:
power / volume-down = PMK8350 (SID 0) PON_HLOS 0x1310 bits 7 / 6 (gen3 PON,
pm8941-pwrkey.c), volume-up = PM6450 (SID 1) GPIO1 0x8810 bit 0, active low.
Still read-only (the only write is EXT_READL on an observer channel) and
still behind sweetkeys=0.

